        <p>174 147 Majority for Armitage and Rigby, 27 points. MATCHES FOR TO-DAY. The following matches will be played to-day : SECOND ROUND. Mersey White Lead 25 v. Fletcher's No. 1 15. TITIRD ROUND.</p>
        <p>Ryland's No. 1 sc. v. Longford Wire No. 2 110. Whitecross (winners 1908) sc. v. L. and N.-W. Rail- way (runners up) sc. Mr. T. O'Brien will act as referee, and Mr. R. Shaw will assist. The gate will be In charge of Mr. F. Dean. __ THE CROSFIELD CHAMPIONSHIP CUP.</p>
        <p>YORKSHIRE V. STAFFORDSIIIR E.—The second of the inter-counry matches in the competition (under the auspices of the British Crown Green Amateur Bowling Association for the Croslleld Championship Cup took place at Wolverhampton do t!laturday. Yorkshire brought a strong learn against Staffordshire, but in the result the borne county won by ten points. The scores were :—Staffordshire, 423 ; Yorkshire, 413. _LANCASHIRE d: CHESHIRE v. YORKSHIRE.</p>
        <p>The opening game between these counties will take place at Halifax on Saturday, June B. Tbe following teams will represent Lancashire and Cheshire :—j. W. G. Coombs (Flixton), H. Connolly (Flixton), C. W. Smith (Flixton), T. Glover (Leigh Railway), J. Grundy (Leigh Railway), H. Harrison (Leigh Railway), IL Williamson, H. Arnold, iunr., and G. Drinkwater (Didsbury), A. Gleave' Gleave and J. Bedworth (Warrington Bull's Hend),T. Ellison and A.'Scott (Warrington Cemetery), S. SAckville (Swinton Liberal), W. Smith (Belmont), .T. Westhend (Harputhev), J. E. Codling (George), T. B. Burgess (Winnington Park), J. Fairhurst (Charlton), P. Talbot (Newton-le-Willows), J. Brooks (Cadishead Railway) and W. Leylancli(RadelitTe.) Reserves: H. Thomason (Knutsford), G. Burnell (Unsworth), T. Dutton (Bowdon), E. Knowles (Urmston Victoria), .1. Antwise (Albion), F. Haslam Measurer, H. Rolle. SECOND TEAM COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Bsdcliffe Withins v. Kersal.—Played--at LowPr Broughton on Saturday. Radcliffe Withins, 221 ; Kersal, 205. _ _ _</p>
        <p>Leigh Railway v. Heat ley Green Dragon.—Played at tho Angel Hotel, Stretford. Leigh Railway, 29: Green Dragon, 182. Swinton Social,2o7 ; Heaton Park, 193. WARRINGTON CCAIE.TERY V. WlGAN.—Played at Newton-le-Willows on Saturday. Scores :</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON CEMETERY. WIGAN. J. E. Harrison (captain) 10 T. Layland R. J. Melbourne II J Connor 2l R Knight lO F. Donnelly 2l pi Gleave 2O J. Hecley 2l w..Cottou w. Roughley . A. Warburton 2l R. Threlfall R. Sunderland 2l W. Battye l4 Iv. Hill 2O J. Naylor 2l A. Forster B. Antrobus , 2l W. Topping 9 F. Yarwood 2' W. Warden .. ..</p>
        <p>210 Majority for Cemetery, 2.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE ASSOCIATION THE CHAMPIONSHIP COMPETITION. WARRINGTON CEMETERY V. ECCLES CROSS KEYS.— These teams met on the green of the Wigan Subscrip- tion Club on Saturd iv. The Warringtonians were in brilliant form, each player winning his g ime indecisive fashion. At the close the winners had a majority of 122 points. Scores : WARRINGTON. ECCLES.</p>
