        <p>he had known deceased upwards of five years. He had had dealings with him on several occasions,and he al says appeared to be very reserved and of n sullen disposition. He did not think he would every enter into conversation voluntarily with anyone. If be bad any trouble he was likely to keep it to himself. There were no circumstances which would arouse suspicion as to the man's death, and he had no cause to suspect foul play. 'Em e jury found a verdict of" Found drowned."</p>
