      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-19_WidnesExaminer_art0112" n="art0112">
        <p>Splendid! Thanks ! !</p>
        <p>One does not hear this or a similar expression of glad feeling as often as one could wish, and its absence is frequently due to man's dilatoriness In exercising a proper care for his health. The habit of procrastination Is strong in human nature. A slight indisposition—a feeling of being a bit " below par"—is given very little heed to, with the result that alarming symptoms often ensue. It is a truism that most sickness takes its rise in a disordered or weak stomach - a torpid state of the liver and bowels inactive kidneys—for any of these derangements</p>
      </div>
