      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-19_WidnesExaminer_art0134" n="art0134">
        <head>WESLEYAN QUARTERLY MEETING.</head>
        <p>WESLEYAN QUARTERLY MEETING.</p>
        <p>The quarterly meeting of the Warrington Methodist Circuit was held at Penketh on Thursday. About seventy sat down to tea and the Penketh friends were thanked for their hospitality on the proposition of Mr. F. Wright seconded by Mr. Wildman. After tea, at the invitation of Mrs. Garnett the members readily availed themselves of the opportunity of inspecting the gardens at Hall Nook which are looking at their best. The business meeting was held in the school- room, the Rev. E. B. Keeling presiding. Amongst those present were :—The Revs. T. Miller, T. Gladding. F. W. Kernick, and John Gunnell, Mr. R. H. Meldrum. and Dr. James Bennett (circuit stewards). The financial position for the quarter was considered quite satisfactory.—The stewards were authorised to invite succegsors to the third and fourth ministers in the year 1911, ministers already having been invited to succeed the Rev. E. B. Keeling and the Rev. Thoinas Millen—A long discus- sion took plAce on Sunday school work. It was reported that there was a considerable increase in Sunday scholars for the year and also in the number of teachers. On the proposition of the Rev. F. W. Kernick, it was decided to commence teachers'</p>
        <p>preparation classes.—The foreign missionary report was submitted and showed a slight increase in the funds for the year.—lt was stated that during the quarter the circuit assessment committee had been called together and practically every chapel in the circuit had voluntarily ircreased its assessment so as to make ample provision for the fourth minister. •</p>
